TEXT 32 -160 Left 2 ;ex01 - FIU short circuits on a fail-operational dual 48 V supply: is each fault isolated selectively, and does the XBW load keep its power?
TEXT 32 -120 Left 1 ;800 V -> 48 V DC/DC --1 m-- [A]-AB-[B]-BC-[C]-CD-[D] --1 m-- 48 V battery | XBW load 1 kW / 1 mF on AB and CD (2 m each) | 10 mOhm short to GND at 1 ms
TEXT 32 -96 Left 1 ;Expected: FID 1 short CD: C (->) and D (<-) open, load on AB | FID 2 short AB: A (->) and B (<-) open, load on CD | FID 3 short BC: B (->) and C (<-) open, load on both | FID 0 golden: nothing trips | load rail always 36..52 V
TEXT 32 -72 Left 1 ;Starts in steady state (eFuses on, DC/DC running in the DC operating point). Probe: V(cr:xu:flt) fault latch, V(cr:xu:hsht) hard short, V(ar:xu:xhcd:t) hard-short timer (trips at 0.5), V(dcdc:il), I(w1:Vs).
